### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### COST -- read before section 7
###
### Every 5 minutes is 288 investigations a day. kimi-k3 is \/MTok in, \/MTok out, thinking
### always on and billed as output. A modest 30k-in/3k-out run is about \.14, so roughly \/day
### -- about \,200/month. A heavier 100k-in/10k-out run is nearer \/day.
###
### The cron is by far the biggest lever: "0 */30 * * * *" is 6x cheaper, "0 0 * * * *" is 12x.
### The account behind the configured key is currently SPENT, so as written this workflow will
### fail every run loudly (non-2xx -> AnalysisImpossibleException -> Failed) rather than silently.
### That is by design, and it makes a quota rejection the cheapest possible proof that the failure
### path reaches Failed instead of silence -- worth doing deliberately once, before funding.
###
### ITERATING ON THE PROMPT
### A running workflow reads the L2 projection from its start time, so editing the assignment
### changes nothing until the workflow is restarted -- the pods keep using the old prompt while the
### row shows the new one. Edit payload -> stop -> start -> confirm the promptHash in the next
### finding changed. That hash is what makes the change confirmable.
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------